Day 9 of hashtag#60DaysOfBuilding 🚀
One of the biggest lessons I learned while developing web applications is that large projects should never be built all at once.
Instead, I followed an iterative development approach:
✅ Version 1 (MVP)
• User profile management
• Food logging system
• Nutrition tracking
• Dashboard with basic insights
✅ Version 2 (Enhanced)
• CSV data upload
• Expanded food database
• Meal planning features
• Health risk analysis
• Advanced analytics and visualizations
This step-by-step process helped me build a more reliable, scalable, and user-friendly application.
The project: NutriScope — a nutrition tracking and analysis web application designed to help users monitor dietary habits, gain insights, and make informed health decisions.
Key Takeaway: Start with a functional MVP, gather feedback, and continuously improve through focused iterations. Small improvements compound into great products.
